WEBVTT

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.160
Asano...

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.200
Where's the money?

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.470
Here are the goods we agreed on.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.510
I have to hand it to you, Black Scissors.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:14.840
I appreciate it.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.550
We're specialists in illegal activities.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.610
Nothing's impossible for us.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.590
This isn't enough.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.420
I can't buy glitter gloss or colored
mascara with this.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.590
I'm sorry.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:30.330
But...

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.300
The limited edition makeup kit is only
sold through tomorrow,

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.660
Asami!

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.700
You can get the money immediately if you go
to some lnternet dating site

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.270
and pick up a pedophilic old man.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:41.700
That's a little...

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.240
A little, my ass.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.070
You might be the class's
number one slowpoke,

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:47.370
but I'm teaching you something useful.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.510
Give me your cell phone.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.410
We said give it!

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.480
No!

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.650
Hand it over!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.510
Are you resisting us, Asami?!

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:17.910
Mommy!

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.460
Wait for me!
Mommy!

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.580
Mikura!

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:34.580
Harada!

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.250
Damn!

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:38.450
You brat!

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.410
Mikura, the police are closing in!

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:53.270
So anyway, I'd like to withdraw
from here quickly!

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.910
So he says. Shall we get out of here
before Pops loses his hair?

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.780
I think I'm going to lose mine too!

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.800
Cover me, Harada!

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:04.920
Harada, wire!

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.020
Gotcha!

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.990
After them!

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.980
Ah, it's so high!

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.730
Bastards!

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.700
There!

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.110
Is the Angel in place?

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.370
She sure is!

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.310
Damn! What's the DSA?

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.780
Who the hell are they?

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:33.340
DSA? Oh!

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.920
Don't say anything to the cops about us.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.900
<i>Norikonda sabaibaru cousutaa</i>

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.870
The survival roller coaster we got on

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.640
There's no need to give up,
run by the highway

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.340
<i>Akirame muyoude run by the highway</i>

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.210
<i>Kimiwa inochi karagara</i>

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.410
You just barely escaped with your life

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.740
<i>Atashitachimo nodoga karakara</i>

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.010
We're thirsty

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.940
<i>Kyokugento mugendai</i>

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.150
Extremities and infinity

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:06.280
<i>Tomo ni sorette mugendai</i>

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.510
Together, they form a fantasy

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.180
<i>Kamaeta me hibana chiri</i>

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:08.380
The eyes, squaring away, are
throwing out sparks

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.210
<i>Oni-san kochira to shita o dasu</i>

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:11.440
"You're it! This way, " you say,
as you stick your tongue out

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:13.440
<i>Wink</i>

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.510
Wink

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.120
<i>Kyouretsuna itamini kansha</i>

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.330
Grateful for the excruciating pain

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.460
<i>Power to iu na no rei de henkan</i>

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.760
I'm restored by a gratitude
known as power

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:25.370
<i>Mou sorosoro okaeri asobareta houga
iinodewa naide shouka</i>

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:25.570
Perhaps it would be better too return soon?

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:34.270
<i>Matsugeno sukima umeruyouni aimeiku</i>

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:34.510
As though filling in the gaps between
the eyelashes, eye make

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:41.580
<i>Kokorono sukima umeruyouni I take</i>

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:41.780
As though filling in the gaps of
my heart, I take

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:46.050
<i>Gekiretsu panchide gyakuni takamaru</i>

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:46.250
On the contrary, the intensity is heightened
by a powerful punch

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:50.520
<i>Yabai shiuchi hodo yokei moechauwa</i>

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:50.590
The worse I'm treated, the more I get fired up

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.890
<i>Mouretsu panchide atashi takaburu</i>

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:55.030
I get worked up over an intense punch

00:03:54.890 --> 00:04:03.320
<i>Sonna koto shite kurete arigatou</i>

00:03:55.030 --> 00:04:03.870
Thank you for doing such a thing

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:05.840
<i>Sukima sukima sukimani mimai</i>

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.040
A gap, a gap, pay a sympathy visit

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.840
<i>Janai janai itainjanai?</i>

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.010
Doesn't it, doesn't it, doesn't it hurt?

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:09.510
<i>Mimai tsurai? ltai? Yabai?</i>

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.780
Is the visit painful? Does it hurt?
Is it dangerous?

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:14.140
<i>lkitai itai shitai, lkitai itai shitai</i>

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:14.450
I want to go, I want to stay, I want to do it

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.250
<i>Mugi-ya</i>

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:20.720
Danger Service Agency...

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:23.390
What about it?

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:28.030
You take the initials. D, S, A! Isn't it?

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.330
So?

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.320
A business executing dangerous matters isn't
something which can be done easily.

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:35.670
That's very true. It certainly is.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.870
Do you know we're called the "Risk Their
Lives Trio" every time we're mentioned?

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:40.040
What are we? A trio of comedians?

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:46.580
<i>Shell of Love</i>

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.840
That sounds like the Chanbara Trio.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.850
They're old. I liked Casey Takamine.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.510
Oh, don't cut there too much.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:51.510
Kuro-baby, do you know what was
inside the barbershop pole?

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.090
Could it be...

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.850
Those macho guys were your underlings?

00:04:57.030 --> 00:05:01.700
The only girl among the Life Risking Trio
seems like she's got great skills.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:02.960
I'm so jealous.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.660
I'll pay for the funeral costs. How much?

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.000
That was an unapproved drug.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.070
Which?

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:10.610
This?

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:11.870
That.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:17.000
It's a rather risky substance being bought
and sold in the black market.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.180
Otherwise, Mr. Kurokawa wouldn't have
been summoned by Mugiyama.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.320
So that group of macho guys were...

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.950
Most likely Black Scissors.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.620
Pops...

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:38.260
He won't come back alive.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:42.740
Again?!

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:44.570
Again?

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:51.340
So, since we messed up your transaction,
what do you want us to do?

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:53.980
Actually, that was...

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.580
Hey, Pops, let's go.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.420
How long does it take to give your hairless
head a haircut, anyway?

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:00.510
Well, time to go. That won't be the
day after tomorrow. Grazie!

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:04.920
I'm sorry. Will you forgive us?

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.600
That was just a job for the both of us.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.650
This time, I'll let it slide.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.600
Sticking your tongue out at
authority, I see.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:23.270
What a nice girl. She's even cute.
Did she really...

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:29.540
You're a poor judge of character, you idiot.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:38.520
That's an imitation.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:42.090
We didn't notice it got swapped!

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:46.200
You're good, scissor macho dude!

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:50.270
I don't care if it's scissors or rock or paper.
Hurry and take it back from them!

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:51.670
There's no time!

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:55.600
I don't ever recall hiring a useless trio.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.080
Say, Missy. What did you just say?

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.770
Uh, hold up, Mikura!

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.180
Ms. Kisami, we can try to
recapture the goods

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:06.990
but if we can't determine the whereabouts,
then we really can't do anything immediately.

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.010
Mr. Asano should have it.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.990
I know where his apartment is,
so go there immediately.

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:14.350
All right, Harada, Mikura...

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.470
This isn't good at all.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.270
What shall we do, Mr. Kurokawa?

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:23.640
You can pout all you want, but it
won't turn into money, Mikura.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.840
But this bitch is belittling us!

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.340
Pisses me off!

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.400
Apologize!

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:30.980
Well...

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.070
He's...

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:35.180
Mr. Asano intends to kill someone.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.980
A man by the name of Takizawa.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.850
Fifteen years ago...

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:47.060
Mr. Asano was a pathology intern
at a university hospital.

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:49.190
What's pathology?

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:54.470
Well, it's an academic discipline where you
examine the cause of illnesses

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.910
and research the outbreak mechanisms. Is
that correct? What are you making me say?

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.010
That's right.

00:07:57.770 --> 00:07:58.770
And?

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:00.230
One day...

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:05.510
Job well done, Asano.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.320
Uh, thank you.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:13.480
I didn't think being an intern
would be this rough.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:18.650
Well, see you later.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.590
She's considerate, and she's a
good-looking woman, that Misaki.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:28.570
Takizawa, you already have a
girlfriend you're dating.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:32.540
I've thought female interns were
all intelligent and ugly,

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:34.200
but there seems to be an exception.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.680
That guy's creepy.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:41.780
That guy, Takizawa, he pretended to be a
good person in front of women.

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:45.480
So it seems like he wasn't popular at all
with his male colleagues.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:48.020
There are a lot of guys like that.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.590
In front of Misaki, that tendency
became especially obvious.

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:54.560
So why is he off to kill Takizawa?

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:59.230
That must mean she chose one of
them, isn't that right?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.300
That's right, she...

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:07.280
I'm telling you I have a date
with Misaki tonight.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:10.770
Anyway, I'm short on cash.
Could I borrow some?

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:14.050
How much?

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:15.920
What the hell is that?

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.680
Why did that Misaki woman
go over to Takizawa?

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:22.450
Then again, Mr. Asano's pathetic!

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:26.490
At the time, she didn't realize

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:29.050
what kind of a person Takizawa was.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.930
Whether she liked it or not, an incident took
place that showed her his true aspect.

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:34.140
Meaning?

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.040
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:38.130
Several weeks later...

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.750
The murder weapon had Takizawa's
fingerprints on it.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:49.850
He had no alibi for the time of the murder,

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:52.320
he disappeared the night of the incident
and as far as suspicion goes,

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:54.720
there was no room for doubt.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:58.330
But the cops couldn't find Takizawa.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:01.300
When you said there's no time, you meant
the statute of limitations?

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:02.600
Yes.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:06.400
Since the statute of limitations is closing in,
Asano started to look for Takizawa.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:10.130
He probably found him by
sacrificing everything.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:11.770
But...

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:15.770
Takizawa had lost all his
memories of the past.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.950
He was afflicted by early-age Alzheimer's.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.950
So that thing we're after is...

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.190
A quick-acting drug for it.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:27.190
I see. So Asano's trying to get
Takizawa's memories back

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:29.560
before the statute of limitations expires.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:32.390
Then he'll ask for the motive
behind the murder and...

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:33.860
Get his revenge.

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:36.260
To imagine, he's continued to think
of her for fifteen years,

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:41.240
and is trying to get revenge for a woman
who never even looked his way.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:45.640
No matter what the reason is, I don't want
Mr. Asano to become a murderer.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:48.970
Please, please stop him! The statute
of limitations is tomorrow, at noon!

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:52.040
That Takizawa guy ought to get offed.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.820
How about if I dispose of him instead?

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.480
Dispose of, Mikura?

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:59.110
We don't happen to be assassins.

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:01.320
I'll pay double the bounty.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.690
<i>9th district</i>

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.820
Your spiky hair stabbed me, you moron!

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:13.070
Mr. Kurokawa, you're speeding too much!

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:15.590
Do you understand we have no time?
Well, do you?

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:26.950
Mikura, Harada?

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:29.540
Here, here. Here, here. This is it.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.120
<i>Asano</i>

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.110
You two, get out of the way.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:46.300
Hey, you! This is going to be reported
to the cops really fast!

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:48.700
Your methods are too reckless.

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:49.830
We don't have time, right?

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:54.270
Mr. Kurokawa, it's deserted.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:58.410
It's still warm.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:01.280
Hey, Mikura!

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:05.220
This is?!

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.430
There he is!

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.030
Asano!

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:25.470
You guys!

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:27.130
All of a sudden, this!

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.110
At this rate, he'll get away!

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:33.910
Mikura, please do something.
While you're at it, give me money.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.880
Then can I hit him with a body shot?

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:39.390
No, no! The target is the goods,
above all else, else, else!

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:41.250
You can do that, right?

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.990
This is different from dealing with the
scissors' macho guys, you know!

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:58.170
If want to live long enough to
eat dinner, don't move!

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:18.860
Asano...

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:46.680
Who are you?

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:49.090
Please don't pick on me.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.360
Do you remember this woman?

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:59.830
I don't know. Who is this woman?

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:04.870
She died, fifteen years ago today.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:08.030
I see. She's in Heaven.

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:11.880
Drink.

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:14.140
If I drink it, you won't hit me anymore?

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:16.120
So drink.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:19.080
All right.

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:24.890
Made it in the nick of time!

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:27.420
But isn't this place dangerous?

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.790
I'm surprised you knew of this place.

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:34.300
The first thing we did when we got to
your apartment was...

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:38.530
We placed a transmitter on your car. We
keep ourselves happy by being prepared.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:42.980
Why don't you stop it?

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:43.970
The hell I will!

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:47.770
It's my job, so I tried to stop you.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.790
But if you want to shoot, go ahead
and shoot that loser.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:52.120
Hey, Mikura!

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:55.520
You know? You know what he did?

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.760
While we sympathize with you,

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:01.990
if you kill him, his motive for murdering Ms.
Misaki will be shrouded in mystery forever.

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:05.070
I don't know who hired you,

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.900
but I knew his reasons in the first place.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:08.070
What?

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.140
I see.

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:11.170
You had your own compelling reasons,

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:12.810
otherwise you wouldn't have kept
this up for fifteen years.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:15.440
Then what was that drug for?

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:19.510
I wanted to get his memories back
and make him atone for his sins.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.220
I wasn't about to kill him when he didn't
have his memories of his past.

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:24.690
Is that so?

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:25.950
That is so.

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:29.280
He had a woman besides Misaki.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:32.460
Not only that,

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.830
he embezzled the research funds
and used them for his own purposes.

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:39.300
But his spending was discovered and he...

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:42.830
I can't do that! That's breaking the law!

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.670
I'm begging you, Misaki.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.840
That body is a world-famous musician, right?

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.610
Once we're done with the pathological
dissection, you know?

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.780
Brain

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:00.760
What are you going to do?

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:02.960
I'm going to sell it to a collector.

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:05.890
Body parts from a celebrity sell for a lot.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.130
Come on, I'm asking you.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:13.170
One wrong move, and there's a possibility I'll
be accused of the deed, and be arrested.

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:16.160
If you love me, help me out
on this one. Okay?

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:18.910
Mikura!

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:20.570
This asshole's an enemy of women!

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:23.080
What's the point of you getting hot
under the collar?

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.580
Let go of me! Let go, Harada! Let go!

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.580
Now, now, calm down.

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:28.050
Aw, nuts.

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:29.050
Mr. Kurokawa...

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:31.150
I'm sorry, is it beyond the hope of recovery?

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.520
Nuts to you too!

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:40.760
But why did he kill Misaki,
a woman so devoted to him?

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:45.100
The cause was Takizawa's other woman.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:46.460
<i>District Chief</i>

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:51.800
Mr. Takizawa, this is about the Paul
Lennon pathological dissection case.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:54.300
Is there something about it?

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:57.110
I've heard a strange rumor.

00:16:57.110 --> 00:16:58.450
It wasn't me!

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:03.050
You and I are the only ones who know
about this. Who else is there?

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:07.560
You're horrible. Do you have any idea how I
felt when I took the specimens out?

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:08.690
You're too cruel.

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:12.990
No, you got scared and sold me out
to the district chief after all.

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:16.960
That has to be it. You're only thinking
about your own safety!

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:18.870
You're talking about yourself!

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:22.130
It all started because there's a
problem with you!

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:25.110
You always place the blame
on someone else,

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.800
and this time you're accusing me!

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:31.510
You're the worst! You're an extreme egoist!

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:33.080
Where are you going?

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:34.550
Going to talk to Asano?

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:39.550
Why did I ever fall for you?

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:42.780
Why you! You treacherous bitch!

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:54.500
I swapped the slide specimens
with someone else's,

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.990
before Misaki took them out.

00:17:57.670 --> 00:17:59.260
What was sold to the collector was...

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:03.270
A specimen of an average Joe
not worth a yen.

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:07.150
You should've settled this
by socking Takizawa.

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:10.410
If you loved her so much, you
should've stolen her from him.

00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:14.420
If I could've done that, this might have
ended without Misaki getting killed.

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:17.990
In this place...

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:21.790
Misaki died here! Her soul is calling you!

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:25.700
Ms. Misaki, you're here, aren't you?

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:28.100
You're the only one who can stop him.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:29.090
What?!

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:34.200
I wonder if I kicked Pops' nads too hard?

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:38.200
This woman...

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:41.200
Mr. Kurokawa, what's the meaning of this?

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.370
Is there such a thing as this?

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:05.740
You've got to be kidding me.

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:08.040
Is this mass hypnotism, Mr. Kurokawa?

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.910
Even I can't explain this.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:15.780
You wasted fifteen years of your own life,
just for the likes of me.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:18.040
You're an idiot, Asano.

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:19.910
It wasn't a waste.

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:24.160
Because I was able to meet you again.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:35.700
You preciously kept that silly little thing?

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:38.160
I couldn't eat it.

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:40.530
I was so happy.

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:45.310
From here on, you'll meet someone.

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:49.910
Someone, somewhere will definitely be in
need of you so please notice her.

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:53.010
You have to forget about me.

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:56.260
I don't need to fall in love again.

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:58.730
Falling in love isn't logical.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:03.560
Well, he won't be able to forget about
Ms. Misaki, but he'll be all right.

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:11.270
Mikura, when you try to see through a man,
think about does he really need you,

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:12.970
or is he thoughtful, or...

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:15.080
Does he know what sadness is?

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:17.440
Right, right. Those are the important things.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:19.480
Mikura, you ought to take note
of such areas and...

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:20.810
Hey, she's transparent!

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.560
Thank you.

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:40.500
You definitely need to find a
fragment of love. Got it?

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:42.370
I'll pick it up.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:52.510
She disappeared.

00:20:52.510 --> 00:20:53.880
This can't be for real.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:56.410
So, this place used to be the
university hospital.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:58.780
Now I understand.

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:02.290
Why does everyone pick on me?!

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:03.980
Pops, I'm firing!

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:23.540
Harada! Pops! You okay?

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:24.880
Somehow!

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.310
We don't look cool though.

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:31.840
Harada, please hurry and climb up.
My hands aren't very strong.

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:34.710
Not good...

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:39.720
No!

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:42.430
I'm going to where Misaki is.

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:46.360
ldiot! You're going to break
your promise to her?!

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:49.460
Let me go near where she is.

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:54.210
Don't make her any sadder than she is.

00:21:58.280 --> 00:22:00.910
Doesn't look good, Mr. Kurokawa.
They'll fall!

00:22:00.910 --> 00:22:02.040
Mikura!

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:06.990
The probability is low, but I've got
no choice but to take it!

00:22:10.990 --> 00:22:12.150
Mikura!

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.570
She really is reckless.

00:22:20.570 --> 00:22:22.230
Is she all right?

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:25.130
Yoo hoo! Pops! Harada!

00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:29.080
It really was a good thing to get her
on our side, Mr. Kurokawa.

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:31.110
Mikura's too awesome.

00:22:31.110 --> 00:22:33.310
Hey! Ms. Misaki! Our payment!

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:38.620
I wonder if we were seeing an illusion?

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:38.620
Well, you talk about standpoints

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:42.990
but that's something you can handle with
your own authority.

00:22:40.450 --> 00:22:42.990
How can you eat so much?

00:22:42.990 --> 00:22:45.190
If you keep yammering about it, I may end up
leaking that particular incident.

00:22:43.160 --> 00:22:46.260
Well, you never know what's going to
happen in this world.

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:50.130
That's right, leaving no details out,
even to your wife.

00:22:46.490 --> 00:22:48.830
The incident this morning,
it's definitely conceivable.

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:53.430
How you can have such a clear-cut
attitude about this is also amazing.

